<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - March 27.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - March 27.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for March 27.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    Mar    206.00    210.50    211.50     224.00</p>
<p>    Apr    204.00    208.50    209.50     224.00</p>
<p>    May    204.00    208.50    209.50     224.00</p>
<p>    Jun    199.50    204.00    205.00     222.50</p>
<p>    Jul    198.00    202.50    203.50     220.50</p>
<p>    Aug    197.00    201.50    202.50     219.50</p>
<p>Note: ASW = Australian Standard White; AH = Australian Hard; PH = Australian Prime Hard; percentages = protein content.</p>
<p>Australian Wheat Board indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1997/98 crop wheat increased A$3.00 per tonne.</p>
<p>	  Indicator Prices in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		  ASW 10 pct protein</p>
<p>National FOB	179.00</p>
<p>Indicator prices on a delivered port basis:</p>
<p> Queensland			   South Australia</p>
<p>    Mackay	  154.50	    Port Adelaide	 156.00</p>
<p>    Gladstone     154.75	    Port Giles	    156.75</p>
<p>    Brisbane	152.50	    Wallaroo		154.50</p>
<p> New South Wales			Port Pirie	    151.50</p>
<p>    Newcastle     154.50	    Port Lincoln	  155.75</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   155.00	    Thevenard	     152.75</p>
<p>Victoria			     Western Australia</p>
<p>    Geelong	 156.00	     Esperance	    159.25</p>
<p>    Portland	155.00	     Albany		 160.25</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    162.25</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    160.25</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
